# sha256 of the release assets bootstrap.sh installs into agent/bin: fd, rg,
# jq, yq, shellcheck and ast-grep. Only jq and ripgrep publish checksums in a
# form this can read at install time, so the pinned versions are recorded here
# and checked exactly the way the Node tarball is.
#
# To pin a new version: change the *_VERSION default in bootstrap.sh, download
# that tool's four assets and add their `shasum -a 256` output below. A version
# that is not listed here still installs - verified against the project's own
# published checksum where there is one, unverified and with a warning where
# there is not.
#
# fd 10.4 and later are built against a macOS SDK newer than the Intel Macs in
# the estate, so x86_64-apple-darwin stays on 10.3.0 - the same pin pi uses.
# ast-grep publishes no musl build, so its Linux assets are the glibc ones.
50d30f13fe3d5914b14c4fff5abcbd4d0cdab4b855970a6956f4f006c17117a3  fd-v10.3.0-x86_64-apple-darwin.tar.gz
